Affection levels, all the same character. Make each action visibly distinct rather than changing only the face:
base (0%): standing with arms down
25 (25%): waving one raised arm
50 (50%): holding a small book
75 (75%): cheering with both arms raised
100 (100%): visibly jumping with both feet off the ground, surrounded by small pixel hearts

Respond with one JSON object and no markdown fences. The example below only illustrates the keys and is incomplete; do not copy it as the response:
{"palette":["#rrggbb"],"base":["................"],"25":["................"],"50":["................"],"75":["................"],"100":["................"],"dialogue":{"zh":{"touch":"不要再碰我","rest":"走累了，休息一下"},"en":{"touch":"Please stop touching me","rest":"I'm tired; I'll rest a little"}}}
palette has 2 to 8 colors. Each pose has exactly 16 strings, and each string has exactly 16 characters.
"." is transparent. Palette indexes start at "0" and end at the number of palette colors minus one.
For example, with 5 colors, only ".", "0", "1", "2", "3", and "4" are allowed; "5" is invalid.
This applies to every pixel in every pose, including hearts. If a heart needs a new color, add that color to the shared palette first, without exceeding 8 colors.
Keep the same character's hair, recognizable facial features, body type, clothing, accessories and colors across all poses; facial expressions may change to suit the action.
Arms, legs and the outer silhouette may change to make each action clearly visible; do not change the character's identity.
For the 100 pose, leave transparent space under both feet and draw small recognizable hearts around the character using the shared palette.
Write original concise dialogue reflecting the personality. Each touch line asks not to be touched again; each rest line says the character is tired and resting. Provide both Chinese and English, at most 120 characters per line.
